My recommendation

The highest priority items to complete before a public release are:

Code-sign the application (OV or EV certificate).
Always build optimized release binaries (cargo build --release / tauri build).
Implement binary hash and release manifest verification for tamper detection.
Sign and verify updates before installation if you add an update mechanism.
Harden configuration and key storage, ensuring secrets are never embedded in the application.

The control-flow flattening warning is the lowest priority. It's an advanced anti-reverse-engineering measure rather than a fundamental security requirement. For an enterprise application like QGuard Messaging, strong cryptography, secure key management, code signing, and integrity verification provide substantially more practical security value.
